Reason: `LambdaSubscriber` is a thin delegating wrapper around user‑provided callbacks and atomic reference management. Its behavior and performance are dominated by the supplied lambdas and the surrounding reactive stream infrastructure, not by any intrinsic algorithmic work within the class itself. Micro‑benchmarking this class in isolation would not yield meaningful insights; performance should be measured at higher‑level components (e.g., Flowable pipelines) where the subscriber is actually used. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark for this class is unnecessary.